{
 "_what": "Item '149 Open 6' (battlegrid-manager docs/status/2026-11-05-contract-149.md, Open 6): does a staged draft echo default knobs - or any value the sender left out - back into its content? The manager's lost-answer recovery (manager/actions/strategy_verify.py, _verify_stage) settles a stage whose answer was lost by matching the re-read draft's content_sha against content_sha(the axes sent): an echoed default would make the two differ and the row wait for the user. Checked offline on every stored stage whose whole sent body and whole read-back are on disk. No platform call was made for this record; B1's read-back is the v0.14.3 probe's (data/audit/stop_band_171_2026-11-12.json).",
 "canonicalForm": "battlegrid-manager manager.risk.radar.canonical / content_sha (manager main d64308d): json.dumps(normalised, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')), every number format(Decimal(str(x)).normalize(), 'f'), null / true / false / strings kept - a key holding null is not dropped",
 "answer": "No echo. 26 read-backs (15 CREATE, 11 UPDATE; contracts 168.2.0, 171.0.0): 0 key(s) added, 0 dropped and 0 value(s) changed against the body sent - for an UPDATE, the union of every stage into the draft, each later stage's axis whole - and content_sha(read) == content_sha(sent) in 26 of 26. The only raw differences are number spellings (-10.0 sent, -10 read back; 10.0 sent, 10 read back), which the canonical form normalises. The bodies sent 177 REPORT columns (counted per read-back) carrying 0 knob keys - OMEGA's Column.wire() drops a knob left None - and keys holding null (bars, benchmarkTicker, exitSide, marketScope, notes, sectionKey, verdict, windowExtreme); every one came back exactly as sent: no default was filled in and no null was dropped. So no echo breaks the manager's lost-answer match. That match, though, compares the WHOLE re-read draft with the axes the LATEST stage sent, so it holds only for a stage that is its draft's only stage, or one that restages every axis the draft holds - 24 of the 26 here, each matching the manager's way (managerMatch). The other 2 do not: the reads at v171/calls.jsonl lines 21 and 23 hold POSITION_MANAGEMENT and TRADE_LEVEL_POLICY, after line 20 staged POSITION_MANAGEMENT alone over a draft holding TRADE_LEVEL_POLICY (draftVersion 4). See managerRecovery.",
 "managerRecovery": "For whoever pins v0.14.3 in battlegrid-manager: the lost-answer match is manager/actions/strategy_verify.py, _verify_stage, lines 160 - 161 (manager main d64308d): read.draft_version > the draftVersion the stage was sent over, and read.content_sha (the WHOLE re-read draft) == content_sha(params.axes, the axes that one stage sent). A stage over a held draft reads back the union of its axes, so the match fails there and the row waits for the user although the stage landed. Here it fails on 2 of 26 read-backs (managerMatch false; lines counted from 0, as every source here): the reads at v171/calls.jsonl lines 21 and 23 hold POSITION_MANAGEMENT and TRADE_LEVEL_POLICY, after line 20 staged POSITION_MANAGEMENT alone over a draft holding TRADE_LEVEL_POLICY (draftVersion 4). Not an echo: against the union of the draft's stages each is canonical-equal. The fix belongs to the manager: compare against the composed draft - the draft the stage was sent over, overlaid by the axes it sent. OMEGA changes nothing for it.",
 "notCovered": "No stored read-back holds a column sent WITH a knob key (knobKeysSent is 0 in every row): L3a / L3b (a BB_LOWER column carrying a knob, 168.3.0) were staged but their read-backs were not kept, and the knob-spelling probes were previews. The read-backs on disk are CREATE drafts at 168.2.0 and 171.0.0 and UPDATE drafts at 171.0.0; an echo a later contract introduced would show here as a canonical difference on the next stored read-back.",
